        "content": "\n**Location**: `use-action-cards.ts:19`, `use-chat.ts:18`\n\n**Problem**: `processedIds` grows forever, never cleared.\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Current: Grows unbounded\nconst processedIds = useRef(new Set<string>());\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  for (const log of snapshot.logs) {\n    if (processedIds.current.has(log.id)) continue;\n    // ...\n    processedIds.current.add(log.id); // Set grows forever!\n  }\n}, [snapshot]);\n```\n\n**Solution**: Use a bounded LRU cache or clear old entries:\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Optimized: Bounded cache with max size\nimport { useRef, useEffect } from \"react\";\n\nclass BoundedSet<T> {\n  private items = new Set<T>();\n  constructor(private maxSize: number) {}\n  \n  add(item: T) {\n    this.items.add(item);\n    if (this.items.size > this.maxSize) {\n      const first = this.items.values().next().value;\n      this.items.delete(first);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  has(item: T): boolean {\n    return this.items.has(item);\n  }\n  \n  clear() {\n    this.items.clear();\n  }\n}\n\nexport function useActionCards(snapshot: A0Snapshot | null) {\n  const processedIds = useRef(new BoundedSet<string>(1000)); // Max 1000 IDs\n  \n  // Clear when context changes\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (snapshot?.context) {\n      processedIds.current.clear();\n    }\n  }, [snapshot?.context]);\n  \n  // ... rest of hook\n}\n```\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Issue 4B: Socket Cleanup",
        "content": "\n**Location**: `use-socket.ts`\n\n**Problem**: Socket event handlers capture closures that could hold stale data.\n\n**Solution**: Already handled well, but ensure refs are used:\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Current implementation is good, just document it\n// The hook properly uses refs to avoid closure issues\n// and cleans up event listeners in the return function\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Redundant Computations",
        "content": "\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Issue 5A: List Virtualization",
        "content": "\n**Problem**: Rendering 100+ table rows causes layout thrashing.\n\n**Location**: All workspace pages with `<Table>` components\n\n**Solution**: Use `@tanstack/react-virtual`:\n\n```typescript\n// src/components/virtualized-table.tsx\nimport { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';\nimport { useRef } from 'react';\n\nexport function VirtualizedTable<T>({ \n  data, \n  columns,\n  rowHeight = 48,\n}: {\n  data: T[];\n  columns: Array<{ key: string; header: string; cell: (item: T) => React.ReactNode }>;\n  rowHeight?: number;\n}) {\n  const parentRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n\n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: data.length,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: () => rowHeight,\n    overscan: 5, // Render 5 extra rows for smooth scrolling\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div ref={parentRef} className=\"h-[600px] overflow-auto\">\n      <div style={{ height: `${virtualizer.getTotalSize()}px`, position: 'relative' }}>\n        {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualRow) => {\n          const item = data[virtualRow.index];\n          return (\n            <div\n              key={virtualRow.key}\n              style={{\n                position: 'absolute',\n                top: 0,\n                left: 0,\n                width: '100%',\n                height: `${virtualRow.size}px`,\n                transform: `translateY(${virtualRow.start}px)`,\n              }}\n              className=\"flex border-b\"\n            >\n              {columns.map(col => (\n                <div key={col.key} className=\"flex-1 px-4 py-3\">\n                  {col.cell(item)}\n                </div>\n              ))}\n            </div>\n          );\n        })}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```typescript\n// In inventory page\n<VirtualizedTable\n  data={filtered}\n  columns={[\n    { key: 'name', header: 'Item', cell: (item) => item.item_name },\n    { key: 'onHand', header: 'On Hand', cell: (item) => parseDisplay(item.on_hand) },\n    // ... more columns\n  ]}\n/>\n```\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Issue 5B: Debounced Search",
        "content": "\n**Problem**: Search filtering runs on every keystroke.\n\n**Solution**: Add debouncing:\n\n```typescript\n// src/hooks/use-debounced-value.ts\nimport { useState, useEffect } from 'react';\n\nexport function useDebouncedValue<T>(value: T, delay: number = 300): T {\n  const [debouncedValue, setDebouncedValue] = useState(value);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => setDebouncedValue(value), delay);\n    return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n  }, [value, delay]);\n\n  return debouncedValue;\n}\n```\n\nUse in pages:\n\n```typescript\nconst [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState(\"\");\nconst debouncedSearch = useDebouncedValue(searchQuery, 300);\n\nconst filtered = useMemo(() => {\n  // Use debouncedSearch instead of searchQuery\n  return data.filter(item => \n    item.name.toLowerCase().includes(debouncedSearch.toLowerCase())\n  );\n}, [data, debouncedSearch]);\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 4
      },
      {
